     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the FDA maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 recommended in one dose, and doses that high raise the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 1,700 mg/day total.\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO with meals**, titrated to the patient's needs.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, tell me the clinical reason and I can enter it with a note, though I'd advise checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
